  "goodToKnow": "Der Söldner is a mercenary, someone who fights for money (der Sold, soldier's pay, which also gave der Soldat). In the Thirty Years' War (1618–1648), mercenary armies (Landsknechte) devastated Germany. Today the Russian Wagner group made Söldner a news word. The Swiss Guard at the Vatican descends from Swiss mercenaries. Plural: die Söldner."
